<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BCP plans real estate sales.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BCP plans real estate sales.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese bank Banco Comercial Portugues (BCP) plans to sell off real estate assets unrelated to financial services, which are valued at about 50 billion escudos ($272.2 million), a senior official said.</p>
<p>&quot;There are about 50 billion escudos (in real estate assets) to be sold off,&quot; Joao Talone, president of BCP's insurance unit Seguros e Pensoes, Gere, told reporters.</p>
<p>He said BCP had so far sold off 60 billion escudos of such assets, including the Colombo shopping centre in Lisbon.</p>
<p>($ = 183.7 Portugese Escudos)</p>
</text>
